Robot stack v1.0: release notes for the open day.
Obstacle stopping passed all 12 scenarios of our simulator test suite [R7].
It has not been tested on the real robot with visitors nearby, so on the open day the robot drives only inside the taped area, at walking pace, with a supervisor holding the emergency stop.
In the simulator, the median localisation error is lower than in last term's release [R8].
We have not measured battery life on the open-day route, so a supervisor checks the battery every hour.
Known limitation: in the simulator, glass and mirrors confuse the range sensor [R9]; keep them out of the area.
